// Lesson 6.2 — Ground Checks: No Infinite Jumps
//
// GROUND TRUTH (read from the teacher's project, Unity 6000.6.0f1):
//   ProjectSettings/TagManager.asset — tags include `Ground` (already defined,
//     the student does not create it) alongside Coin, Enemy, Axe, Spikes and
//     GroundCheck. There is NO `Ground` layer.
//   Assets/_Scenes/Platformer.unity — the Grid's `Collision` tilemap is tagged
//     `Ground` and carries TilemapCollider2D + CompositeCollider2D + a STATIC
//     Rigidbody2D. `Cave Exit` carries the SAME three components and is
//     Untagged — it is solid and it is not ground.
//   Assets/Scripts/PlayerController.cs — the built ground check:
//         int jumpsRemaining;  int maxJumps = 1;
//         Start(): else { ... jumpsRemaining = maxJumps; print(jumpsRemaining); }
//         Update(): if (Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.J) && jumpsRemaining >= 1)
//                   { Jump(); jumpsRemaining -= 1; }
//         OnCollisionEnter2D(Collision2D other)
//                   { if (other.gameObject.CompareTag("Ground")) { jumpsRemaining = maxJumps; } }
//   It is a COLLISION CALLBACK on a TAG. Not a raycast, and not a layer.
//
// WHY THIS PAGE LOOKS DIFFERENT FROM THE OLD ONE: the old 6.2 taught a
// `Physics2D.Raycast` against a `Ground` LAYER, with a `GroundCheck` empty
// child as the origin. The built code does none of that. Aram's ruling —
// "Keep my trigger radius and then in ground check we are going to do raycast
// on a future day. Not yet." — so the raycast is named once, as the thing 7.2
// comes back to, and never built here. The layer argument goes with it: the
// built check compares a TAG, so this page teaches the tag honestly and says
// why a raycast would have needed a layer instead.
//
// SCAFFOLDING: GUIDED (level 2). asks.ts agrees. Two numbers, one gate, one
// decrement and one refill are given; exactly one line is the student's — the
// refill, which is the only line that has to say "the jump is rechargeable".
//
// PROTECTED BLOCKS — answer-box ids are POSITIONAL (src/lib/formify.ts).
// The Socratic block is still the document's first, still has exactly three
// questions, and the decompose block still has the same id. Nothing is added
// above a surviving box.
//
// CHECK 11: no bare Unity method names in prose — every one is written as a
// call (`CompareTag()`, `OnCollisionEnter2D()`, `Update()`).
